+---
+description: "Manage saved memory and extraction from general settings."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings-memory
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Open Cross-conversation memory in General settings to search and filter records, add or edit a record, enable or disable it, or delete it.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Preferences and editing](#preferences)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="preferences"></a>
+## Preferences and editing
+
+The master switch and automatic extraction both default to off. Enable the master switch for retrieval and saving. Automatic extraction makes a separately billed request using the current model. The panel shows extraction status for open sessions and can retry a failed or canceled extraction while its session is idle. The mode settings page opens the same panel with a mode filter. Status notifications remain visible after closing the dialog.
+
+The list updates after the Host acknowledges a change. The controller retains drafts across navigation and version conflicts. Errors use localized messages with retry guidance.
+
+The scope, type and mode menus support keyboard navigation, themes and focus restoration. Only the application owner can manage records. Deleting a conversation keeps its memories. Deleting a memory preserves the logs of earlier conversations.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+Indirectly, through the management API that changes the records and preferences used in future conversations.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Opening the panel does not change a model request. The memory service logs the revisions it later injects.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The panel distinguishes available, missing and unverified sources. It does not open the source conversation.
+- Refresh to read extraction status from open sessions. Retrying requires an open, idle session.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance reference</summary>
+
+The [management Remote](../../api/memory-controller/README.md) owns authorization and version checks.
+
+The client event `memory/open-manager(mode?, workspace?, seed?)` opens the manager with optional mode and workspace selections and a draft for review.
+
+</details>
