+
+# 2026-11-25-released-composer-predictions
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-25-released-composer-predictions.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Recognizes the input/prediction event written by released DSHU v4 composers.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-25-released-composer-predictions
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:input/prediction"
+    previous: null
+    after: "f3072bbcf9af7b706e37ce7ac1df223c58ec2c4512e8be71c4b42e053f343d7f"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+The v4 reader keeps the original event, including optional request details, outcome and token usage. Drafts and suggestions have no surface operation. Reopening the log does not submit either as a message. The reader still rejects unknown required event types.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The release-data fixture calls the shipped composer writer, reopens its compressed log with the candidate, appends a turn and checks both prediction events and the projected messages after restart. The JSONL admission suite also covers a prediction without request identity or usage, and an unknown required event.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
